# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real text-to-video generation
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NO KEY REQUIRED TO START. With nothing set, the studio renders every clip
# on the free on-device engine — entirely in the browser, no upstream call,
# no account, no cost.
#
# Setting one of the keys below upgrades generation to a hosted AI video
# model. They are tried in this order, and the first one with a key wins:
#   GEMINI_API_KEY  -> Google Veo 3.1  (up to 4K, native audio)
#   FAL_KEY         -> Veo / Sora / Kling / Wan / Hailuo / LTX
#   REPLICATE_API_TOKEN -> Wan, Veo, MiniMax, LTX
#   RUNWAYML_API_SECRET -> Runway Gen-4
#   LUMAAI_API_KEY  -> Luma Ray 2
#
# 4K note: only Veo 3.1 and Luma Ray 2 advertise 4K. On every other model the
# studio requests 1080p and the 4K button is disabled rather than upscaled.

# GEMINI_API_KEY=
# FAL_KEY=
# REPLICATE_API_TOKEN=
# RUNWAYML_API_SECRET=
# LUMAAI_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Self-hosted (your own GPU) — outranks every key above once configured.
# See docs/self-hosting.md and docker/ for a one-command setup of either.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ComfyUI backend — bundles LTX-Video 2B and Wan 2.1 T2V, selected by
# COMFYUI_MODEL. Do not point this at an unauthenticated ComfyUI: put a
# reverse proxy in front (docker/ ships one) and set COMFYUI_TOKEN to match.
# COMFYUI_URL=
# COMFYUI_TOKEN=
# COMFYUI_MODEL=ltx

# Standalone CogVideoX server (docker/cogvideox-server/) — a different
# open model, not ComfyUI-based.
# COGVIDEOX_URL=
# COGVIDEOX_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real footage, no AI, no GPU, free forever: searches Pexels' stock library
# for a clip matching the prompt's keywords and plays that clip directly.
# NOT a generation model — it can only return footage that actually exists,
# so it's genuine for "a dog running in snow" and a miss for anything that
# isn't real (a fictional creature, an impossible scene). Ranks below every
# provider above (they actually depict the prompt); above nothing configured.
# Free key, no card, no expiry: https://www.pexels.com/api/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# PEXELS_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Song Studio (nav -> Audio) — full songs with vocals, a self-hosted
# SongGeneration Studio server (docker/songgen-server/). Separate from video:
# there's no free on-device fallback for singing. See docs/song-generation.md.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# SONGGEN_URL=
# SONGGEN_TOKEN=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Optional: pin a specific model instead of the provider default.
# Model ids move as providers ship new versions; these let you follow a rename
# without a code change.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# GOOGLE_VEO_MODEL=veo-3.1-generate-preview
# FAL_VIDEO_MODEL=fal-ai/veo3
# REPLICATE_VIDEO_MODEL=wan-video/wan-2.2-t2v-fast
# RUNWAY_VIDEO_MODEL=gen4_turbo
# RUNWAY_API_VERSION=2024-11-06
# LUMA_VIDEO_MODEL=ray-2

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Supabase (auth / project persistence) — optional
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=https://your-project.supabase.co
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=your-supabase-key
